@workers_governments
title: Workers' governments
subtitle: Press for workers' governments in the states. · dev: kf_right_strength +6, kf_left_dissent +3
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; kf_right_strength += 6; kf_left_dissent += 3

Brandler argues that workers' governments in Saxony and Thuringia would put police and administration at the party's disposal, and that this is the way to bring SPD workers with us. The Left says it only ties us to the same SPD leaders who put down the revolution.

@argue_moscow
title: Argue our case in Moscow
subtitle: The German party's view must be heard by the Comintern. · dev: trust +5, kf_apparatus_dissent +2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; comintern_trust += 5; kf_apparatus_dissent += 2

Brandler travels to Moscow and argues the German case. The Comintern's leaders listen, and note what they hear. The Moscow apparatus in our own party dislikes having its role described by someone else.
